WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.660
A limited liability partnership selling IT services.

2
00:00:05.281 --> 00:00:19.971
A person, an HUF, a partnership firm, an LLP, an AOP or BOI, or a company - each card starts its own filing. A trust says Not yet, with what to do meanwhile.

3
00:00:20.577 --> 00:00:33.177
An LLP: services, GST, full books. No presumptive card - an LLP cannot use 44AD. ITR-5.

4
00:00:33.781 --> 00:00:48.801
The form follows from the picks, with its reason in one line - ITR-1, 2, 3 or 4 for a person or an HUF, ITR-5 for a firm, an LLP or an AOP, ITR-6 for a company.

5
00:00:49.421 --> 00:01:03.721
Needed, good to have, and what you type in - each with what it is and where to get it: TRACES, the AIS, your employer, CAMS or KFintech, the GST portal, the firm's deed and its books.

6
00:01:04.327 --> 00:01:14.167
The GST certificate and the LLP agreement. The constitution says Limited Liability Partnership - it fits the card.

7
00:01:14.781 --> 00:01:21.241
The client is made as an LLP; the designated partners come from the agreement.

8
00:01:21.842 --> 00:01:29.042
Then the 26AS - clients' fees with 194J TDS - and the income statement.

9
00:01:29.639 --> 00:01:39.959
No tax audit, the books tagged, the 26AS in - straight on to Compute & close, with the fees set against the 26AS.
